.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt UPGETTY 1
.Os UP-Term
.Sh NAME
.Nm upgetty
.Nd a Unix-style login on the serial port
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Cm BAUD Ar n
.Op Cm RTSCTS
.Op Cm UNIT Ar n
.Op Cm DEVICE Ar name
.Op Cm ROWS Ar n Cm COLS Ar n
.Op Cm TERM Ar name
.Op Cm SHELL Ar command
.Op Cm LOOP
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
gives the far end of a serial line \(em a null-modem cable or a USB serial
adapter, with
.Ql screen /dev/ttyUSB0 19200 ,
minicom or PuTTY there \(em a shell on a real tty: line editing, the window
size
.Pq Li stty rows/cols ,
and full-screen programs such as less, nano, vim and tmux.
Ctrl-C, Ctrl-Z and Ctrl-\e work as on a Unix tty: only the bytes 0x03,
0x1A and 0x1C cross the cable, and the Amiga end turns them into signals
for the running program.
Unlike
.Ql NewShell AUX: ,
every byte arrives as it was sent.
.Bl -tag -width "DEVICE name"
.It Cm BAUD Ar n
The line speed; 19200 when not given.
.It Cm RTSCTS
Hardware flow control: needed for 115200, with a cable that carries RTS
and CTS.
.It Cm UNIT Ar n , Cm DEVICE Ar name
The serial device and its unit.
.It Cm ROWS Ar n , Cm COLS Ar n
The far end's window size.
.It Cm TERM Ar name
The terminal type the shell is given.
.It Cm SHELL Ar command
The program to start instead of vsh.
.It Cm LOOP
Start a new shell each time one ends.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl upgetty LOOP
.Dl upgetty BAUD 115200 RTSCTS LOOP
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr rz 1 ,
.Xr sz 1 ,
.Xr vsh 1
